## 4. Handling Asymmetric Shading in Reference Views (Pre-CMY Delighting)

Real component crops (`14_ArmGuard/components/Arm_Flare/cmy/C_005/master.png`) carry baked studio lighting (bright specular streak on one cheek, soft shadow falloff across the bevel). Two immediate bugs arise in CMY 1.0:
- Yellow Sobel/DoG extraction triggers more strongly on the high-contrast lit rim than on the identical mirrored shadow rim, skewing symmetry estimation and `field_u` ridge confidence.
- Feeding lit `master.png` into downstream texturing bakes directional shadows twice (once in `BaseColor`, once in the game engine light).

**Solution Tested in [`poc5_delight_and_uv_height_bridge.py`](/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-meshes/Audit_14-November-2026/poc/poc5_delight_and_uv_height_bridge.py):**
- Convert foreground `master.png` (inside `mask.png`, background filled with neutral mean grey to prevent boundary ringing!) through `DelightBaseColor.delight` with safe mask-bounded exposure normalization.
- Compare `CheckAiHeight.measure` directional coherence and Left-vs-Right bilateral symmetry error (`|I(x) - I(2*cx - x)|` inside `mask & flip(mask)`) BEFORE and AFTER delighting.
- Extract `DelightBaseColor` + straight-strip `HeadlessM1`-compatible UV sheet + Copernicus formula `BaseColor`, `Height`, `Normal`, `Roughness`, `AO` (`ORM`) directly on the PoC 2 `Arm_Cuff` & PoC 4 `Forearm_Limb` meshes.

